## Control {{controlId}}: Ensure Personnel Are Trained to Carry Out Information Security Duties

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization provides role-based security training within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through specialized training curricula for administrators, developers, and users documented in "Role-Based Security Training Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**Role-Specific Training Tracks:**

**System Administrators:**
- M365 GCC High security administration (Entra ID, Intune, Exchange Online, SharePoint)
- Privileged access management and PIM activation procedures
- Security incident handling and forensic evidence preservation
- Configuration management and change control procedures
- Separate privileged and standard user accounts; privileged roles activated only for the task at hand and for a limited time
- Break-glass (emergency access) account procedures and post-use review

**Security Officers (ISSO/ISSM):**
- CMMC Level 2 assessment preparation and evidence collection
- Risk assessment methodology (NIST SP 800-30)
- Continuous monitoring program management
- POA&M development and tracking

**General Users:**
- CUI identification, marking, and handling per 32 CFR Part 2002
- Acceptable use of M365 GCC High services
- Phishing and social engineering recognition
- Incident reporting procedures

**CUI Handlers:**
- CUI identification, including CUI Basic vs. CUI Specified and recognizing CUI that is not yet marked
- Applying Microsoft 365 sensitivity labels and complying with DLP policies when sharing CUI
- Approved CUI storage locations and transmission methods (no personal cloud storage or text messaging)
- CUI disposal and media sanitization (see MP.L2-3.8.3)

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Assign role-based training upon role assignment; track completion; update curricula annually; retrain on role change or privilege escalation
- **Frequency:** Initial training upon role assignment; annual refresher per role
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Role-Based Security Training Policy v1.0, Training Completion Matrix

**Review Frequency:** Annually by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine role-based training assignments, completion records, curricula content review history, and role-specific competency assessments.

